{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791438662,"nonce":"ljLPa/JYYqKYskF3O7LBZ9j5gyA=","message":"Load-monitored follow-up, 2026-10-08\n\nRepeated the two landed arithmetic optimizations using the exact fdf137cb52c3dc468a8c52d5bc88b1a6431a3a1c zylua snapshot, LLVM disabled, affinity 0-7, 11 randomized repetitions per arm, and same-executable disable flags. All checksums matched LuaJIT. One-second CPU/process/pressure/temperature samples accompanied the runs.\n\nMedian wall milliseconds (optimization disabled / enabled / LuaJIT):\n  branchy 20M: 82.566 / 75.668 / 163.244\n  branchy 100M: 327.808 / 296.903 / 811.550\n  collatz 299999 starts: 201.595 / 155.616 / 136.675\n  collatz 1499999 starts: 1019.925 / 763.830 / 730.094\n\nMedian kernel milliseconds (disabled / enabled):\n  branchy 20M: 61.198 / 55.318\n  branchy 100M: 306.117 / 276.375\n  collatz 299999: 179.758 / 136.243\n  collatz 1499999: 998.194 / 743.953\n\nThe improvement direction reproduces, but this is not a fully idle-machine verdict. Across 61 samples, observed persistent external processes used a median 0.566 CPU core, maximum 0.656 core, mostly Firefox and gnome-shell. The package temperature sensor reached 99 C. These samples can miss short-lived processes. A separate subsequent check collected thermal-throttle counters before/after five seconds idle and ten long Collatz invocations; no counters increased during that check. That does not establish whether throttling occurred during the earlier comparison.\n\nShort wall time remains poor: branchy 10k enabled 16.790 ms versus LuaJIT 1.872; Collatz 100 enabled 22.383 versus LuaJIT 1.962. No broad Python improvement is established. Before the load caveat, a nine-pair nbody confirmation found the apparent regression did not reproduce: five trials disabled/enabled wall 138.745/137.679, fifty trials 339.552/335.519; those observations remain provisional because contemporaneous load was not recorded.\n\nEvidence on NUC: /tmp/zyntax-load-confirm-20261008/{metadata.json,results.json,load.jsonl,thermal-confirm.json}; driver /tmp/zyntax-load-confirm.py. Local copy: /tmp/zyntax-load-confirm-20261008-local. Earlier Python confirmation: /tmp/zyntax-power2-nbody-confirm.json. Keep earlier all-kernel rankings and marginal performance-based experiment decisions provisional; a new ranking needs comparable load-monitored runs of every runtime.","files":null}]}